# The vendor's binaries -- the package and its shared libraries -- are committed as ordinary
# blobs. That is 35 MB of files that never change, which git stores in about 21 MB of pack.
# LFS would only pay off if many vendor versions accumulated, and it costs a dependency on
# every clone: git lfs pull, remote quota, and LFS objects in the backup.
#
# -text stops CRLF conversion. -diff keeps their bytes out of textual diffs, which is what
# diff=lfs used to do.
vendor/originals/**/*.deb -text -diff
vendor/originals/**/*.xlsx -text -diff
vendor/originals/**/*.docx -text -diff
vendor/sdk/**/*.so* -text -diff

# The vendor's recorded trajectories are CRLF and are compared byte-for-byte by
# tools/verify.sh, so they must never be normalised.
vendor/sdk/**/*.csv -text

# Text we author, or that we generate for review, should diff cleanly.
*.py   text
*.md   text
*.json text
*.yml  text
*.yaml text
*.sh   text
*.cpp  text
*.hpp  text
